report.summary:
WP-36 round 3: all three verified major findings and the four minor findings are fixed in internal/config/subst and internal/config/overlay. For each finding the whole class was fixed and every member has its own test.

Finding 1 (the lenient re-read was quadratic): scan.go is now a streaming scanner, scanEach. It allocates nothing per expression and keeps three forward-only searches (next $, next } and next ${), so each byte is read a bounded number of times in strict and lenient mode alike. Strict reasons are unchanged; a } that comes after the next ${ never closes a default. Searches and name reads report their bytes to the meter at least every 64 KiB. One work unit is 64 bytes read, written or compared, so Yield now runs inside long scalars. Class members fixed together:
- the '}' search of unterminated and nested defaults;
- long names read in one go (now windowed);
- the lenient re-read used by the credential detectors;
- per-expression segment memory (a 262,144-expression scalar used to allocate 83 MB);
- secretLike, which allocated through strings.ToLower on every expression;
- the detector and header passes.
scaleShapes gained seven malformed shapes with byte-based units, three hint shapes and one output shape. Also added: TestYieldInsideLongScalar, TestSearchWindow, TestScanMemory, TestScanMatchesReference and FuzzScan, which compares scanEach against the old quadratic scanner, kept in the tests as the reference.

Finding 2 (the hint cost was quadratic and paid at every occurrence): the new hint.go gives exactly diag.Nearest's answer over the sorted HintNames (TestHintsMatchNearest, FuzzHints, TestOSAWithin) at linear cost. Class members:
- the case-insensitive EqualFold pass is now one simple-fold-key map lookup (Kelvin sign, long s and invalid bytes are covered);
- the OSA distance strips the common prefix and suffix, runs in a band of the distance limit (at most 3) with three rows of 7 cells, and stops early;
- names longer than the longest HintNames entry plus 3 bytes are skipped;
- each distinct name is computed once per Substituter through a mutex memo capped at MaxDiagnostics names;
- the index is built lazily;
- all hint work is charged to the work counter.
Tests: TestHintCost (allocation and work-unit bounds, including 20,000 names sharing a long prefix), TestHintMemo, TestOSAEarlyStop, TestOSAAffix, TestCommonAffix.

Finding 3 (amplification was unbounded): Options.MaxOutputBytes (DefaultMaxOutputBytes = 64 MiB, the value of MaxSourceBytes) bounds the text one render writes, counted by the Substituter across all calls with an overflow-free compare-and-swap counter. The size of a scalar is checked before its text is built, so nothing is allocated past the limit. When the limit is spent, the call returns LimitDiagnostic alone: an RZ-CFG-001 error with no file, resource or path. Spent() is sticky and deterministic: it is set exactly when the sum over all resources passes the limit, whatever the order or worker count. Counted class members: values, defaults (taken for unset or empty variables), literal parts, and $${ unescaped in free and forbidden positions. The detectors now read authored text only, so amplified text is never scanned. Tests: TestOutputLimitHostile (allocation bounded), TestOutputLimitBoundary and TestOutputLimitWorkers.

Minor 1: the package doc and the TestForbiddenPositions comment now say that mapping keys and the envelope fields are never substituted or unescaped. A neverSubstituted hint ("... so $${ is not an escape there") now covers keys, apiVersion and kind (no-schema path) and metadata.name; the old hint "write $${" in those positions was wrong. metadata.name holding $${ is now RZ-CFG-011 under 01 req 16 (TestNeverSubstituted).

Minor 2: both RZ-CFG-013 credential rules now read the authored runs (eachRun): literal text plus every default, taken or not, cut at each ${NAME} without a default. Variable values are never read. The success path, the undefined path and the malformed path now agree, and the header-literal rule uses the framing test on defaults. FuzzSubst's reference was updated and a free-position warning property added. New TestAuthoredReading cases cover the finding's examples: untaken credential defaults, the case A/B pair and framing-only defaults; four TestCredentialWarnings rows changed accordingly.

Minor 3: added Substituter.ApplyWith(res, yield) for a per-worker Yield (Apply equals ApplyWith with Options.Yield), with Substituter and Options docs to match. The overlay Options and Yield docs now say each worker passes its own copy, and that a Yield shared across goroutines must be safe for concurrent use. Tests: TestApplyWithYield, TestCheckBaseWorkerYield, and an atomic Yield count in TestConcurrentCheckBase.

Minor 4: the overlay package, CheckBase and Apply docs now name all three consequences of an unresolved dispatch, and TestUnresolvedDispatch pins each one, with exact texts for the RZ-CFG-006 from CheckBase and the RZ-CFG-005 from a changed dispatch.

Coverage is 99.7% for subst and 99.4% for overlay.

contractRequests:
WP-55 (internal/config/loader) scope in 00-architecture.md 4.4 and wps.json, to be stated:
(a) build one subst.Substituter per render, shared by all stage E workers;
(b) each worker calls ApplyWith(res, yield) with its own yield function holding that worker's time since its last runtime.Gosched (01 req 53), and passes overlay.CheckBase its own Options copy whose Yield does the same;
(c) when Substituter.Spent() is true after stage E, the stage's result is one LimitDiagnostic and the stage's other diagnostics and resources are dropped, because which calls finished before the limit was spent depends on scheduling;
(d) pass the run's diagnostic cap as subst/overlay Options.MaxDiagnostics.
